[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Non-vacuity
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Each Phase B test first runs the vector through the **C** `.so` alone and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    144[0m:[38;5;10m[49m asserts the C accepts it *and* decodes it to a plaintext / pixel array computed
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    145[0m:[38;5;10m[49m independently of both implementations (`common::deflate::apply` for DEFLATE
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m token streams, `expected_pixels` for PNGs). Only then is the Rust `.so` compared
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m against the C. So a bug in the generator cannot make the two "agree on garbage".
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    149[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Two places relax this deliberately, and say so in the test:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Stored DEFLATE blocks.** `cp_stored` derives the source pointer from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `cp_ptr`, whose bit accounting is off by a byte for some input lengths (the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   final-word path in `cp_peak_bits` adds `bits_left` rather than
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    154[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `last_bytes * 8`). The C therefore copies from the wrong offset. Those rows
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    155[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   assert "C accepts, and Rust matches C exactly" (`ok_loose`) rather than
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    156[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   "C produces the plaintext" — the C is ground truth.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    157[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Short PLTE** (row 30). `cp_depalette` indexes `plte[c*3]` with no bound on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    158[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `c`, so a short palette makes the C read the bytes following the chunk. Both
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    159[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   libraries are handed an identical, deterministically padded buffer, so the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    160[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   requirement is agreement.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    161[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    162[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Additional coverage beyond the table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    163[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    164[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/isolated.rs` adds 3694 subprocess cases that also fall under Phase B for
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    165[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the ones that succeed, including 26 cases where a run-length code overruns the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    166[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C's `uint8_t lens[288+32]` into its own stack frame by up to 35 bytes, the C
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    167[0m:[38;5;10m[49m still decodes the block, and the Rust translation's emulated frame produces
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    168[0m:[38;5;10m[49m byte-identical output. That is the positive test for the most delicate part of
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    169[0m:[38;5;10m[49m the translation.
